{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And they sent the striped tunic.</b> This means by means of a messenger, and then the messengers would bring it to their father. And some say: they dragged it — like מעבור בשלח and like שלחיך פרדס — and they themselves brought it to their father, so that they would have a pretext to say, 'A wild beast has devoured him.'" "<b>Recognize now, etc.</b> Judah said it, and therefore he was punished in the same language for the matter of Tamar, as it is written: הכר נא למי החותמת."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:34.145617436Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}